Another key tip is to prioritize data.

1033
00:42:51,260 --> 00:42:51,480
Yes.

1034
00:42:52,020 --> 00:42:54,510
Numbers are the foundation of financial communication.

1035
00:42:54,610 --> 00:42:55,110
Absolutely.

1036
00:42:55,270 --> 00:42:58,670
You've got to back up your statements with those solid facts and figures.

1037
00:42:58,850 --> 00:42:59,880
Back it up with data.

1038
00:43:00,180 --> 00:43:02,440
Don't just say, we're doing well this year.

1039
00:43:02,500 --> 00:43:04,200
Show them the evidence.

1040
00:43:04,220 --> 00:43:04,700
Exactly.

1041
00:43:05,080 --> 00:43:08,270
Instead of these vague claims, use specific data points.

1042
00:43:08,470 --> 00:43:09,270
Perfect.

1043
00:43:09,250 --> 00:43:17,920
You could say this year's EBITDA grew by 25 percent, exceeding our projections and demonstrating the effectiveness of our new growth strategy.

1044
00:43:18,160 --> 00:43:20,860
OK, concrete numbers, specific examples.

1045
00:43:21,140 --> 00:43:23,200
It's about painting a clear picture with the data.

1046
00:43:23,800 --> 00:43:28,530
What else should our listeners keep in mind as they're navigating this world of financial communication?

1047
00:43:28,790 --> 00:43:29,950
Active voice is your friend.

1048
00:43:30,450 --> 00:43:30,670
OK.

1049
00:43:30,690 --> 00:43:33,930
It makes your communication more direct, more dynamic and more engaging.

1050
00:43:34,070 --> 00:43:34,530
Gotcha.

1051
00:43:34,550 --> 00:43:37,400
Instead of saying the report was analyzed by the finance team,

1052
00:43:37,700 --> 00:43:39,580
Say the finance team analyzed the report.

1053
00:43:39,820 --> 00:43:40,000
Right.

1054
00:43:40,060 --> 00:43:45,140
So it seems like a small change, but it makes a big difference in terms of clarity and impact.

1055
00:43:45,160 --> 00:43:45,600
Exactly.

1056
00:43:46,120 --> 00:43:50,590
It puts the focus on the action, not on this like passive receiver of the action.

1057
00:43:50,670 --> 00:43:50,950
Right.

1058
00:43:50,990 --> 00:43:52,750
It's like taking ownership of the statement.

1059
00:43:52,920 --> 00:43:58,830
And while it's great to expand your financial vocabulary, remember to use jargon carefully.

1060
00:43:58,870 --> 00:43:59,550
Okay.

1061
00:43:59,570 --> 00:44:03,140
You don't want to overwhelm your audience with overly technical language.

1062
00:44:03,300 --> 00:44:03,510
Right.

1063
00:44:03,920 --> 00:44:10,650
The goal is to communicate effectively, not to impress people with, you know, your knowledge of obscure acronyms.

1064
00:44:10,850 --> 00:44:14,310
Know your audience, adapt your language, make sure everyone's on the same page.

1065
00:44:14,430 --> 00:44:15,110
Exactly.

1066
00:44:15,090 --> 00:44:19,020
Speaking of learning new things, I'm a big believer in practice.

1067
