1068
00:44:24,770 --> 00:44:26,170
I love that that's a great strategy.

1069
00:44:26,250 --> 00:44:26,630
You know?

1070
00:44:26,650 --> 00:44:27,110
Yeah.

1071
00:44:27,150 --> 00:44:32,520
The more you practice using these terms and phrases in context, the more natural and effortless they'll become.

1072
00:44:33,120 --> 00:44:40,040
Find opportunities to discuss financial topics with colleagues, friends, or even just rehearse, you know, different scenarios in your mind.

1073
00:44:40,100 --> 00:44:40,660
Exactly.

1074
00:44:40,700 --> 00:44:42,120
Don't be afraid to experiment.

1075
00:44:42,890 --> 00:44:43,470
Talk it out.

1076
00:44:44,090 --> 00:44:44,750
Make it your own.

1077
00:44:44,890 --> 00:44:46,610
It's like learning any new skill.

1078
00:44:46,730 --> 00:44:48,870
The more you practice, the more confident you become.

1079
00:44:49,090 --> 00:44:54,060
And remember, mastering financial English isn't just about, you know, sounding impressive.

1080
